# Bento / TAILORx

- Adapter class/app key is `Bento`; fixture is `bento`; object repository,
  testcase, and input folders are named `BENTO`. Preserve this case distinction.
- Expected data uses Neo4j Cypher. Verify the TAILORx model and relationship
  directions; do not reuse another portal's participant or file graph blindly.
- `open_cases()` opens Cases exploration. Tabs are Cases, Samples, Files; stats
  also include Programs, Arms, and Assays. Read the adapter's exact tab keys.
- Arm filters use `Filter/Arm` and `select_arm()`. Other examples include
  `Filter/Diagnosis`, `Filter/TissueType`, and `Filter/FileAssociation`.
- Read `Commons/bento_arm_filters.py` for the existing arm/facet matrix. Keep
  cases under `Testcases/BENTO/arm-a/` through `arm-d/`, not a new studies layout.
- Age is a range interaction implemented by `set_age_range()` and repository
  `other` inputs; do not treat it as a checkbox or add invented group fields.
- Preserve Cases/Samples/Files column rules, including selection/Access columns.
- Follow `expected-data.mdc`: narrow to the intended arm/cohort before expanding
  samples/files, prevent join fan-out, and validate Neo4j plans and execution time.
